@@ -8,8 +8,10 @@ Create's action-specific adapter runs authenticate, resolve tenant, authorize, m
 
 Create accepts exact `application/json` and at most 1024 bytes/depth 8. Exact fields `id:int`, `name:string`, `email:string` all pass shape/type validation before values. Positive IDs are client-selected; names are 1–80 UTF-8 bytes with no ASCII controls or trim padding; email is <=254 bytes and an unchanged PHP FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL result. No normalization; duplicate JSON keys retain PHP's last-value limitation. Shape/type failure is generic 400; unacceptable value 422; body overflow 413; media 415. Named conflict is 409. Validation occurs before protected SQL. Success is 201 with exact `data:{id,name,email}`. See data for transactional semantics.
 
-List accepts only optional canonical positive decimal `after_user_id` within PHP_INT_MAX. Missing means first page; null, empty, arrays, unknown keys, leading zeroes and overflow fail 400 before protected SQL. One query fetches <=21, immediate `UserSummary` projection validates every row, and I/O-free mapping emits <=20 with `next_after_user_id` set only when lookahead exists. SQLite returns native integer IDs; strings are rejected. Ordering is ascending ID, static-fixture keyset pagination, no concurrent snapshot guarantee.
+List accepts optional literal `search` and optional canonical positive decimal `after_user_id` within PHP_INT_MAX. Missing means first page; null, empty, arrays, unknown keys, leading zeroes and overflow fail 400 before protected SQL. One query fetches <=21, immediate `UserSummary` projection validates every row, and I/O-free mapping emits <=20 with `next_after_user_id` set only when lookahead exists. SQLite returns native integer IDs; strings are rejected. Ordering is ascending ID, static-fixture keyset pagination, no concurrent snapshot guarantee.
 
 Health/404/405 retain explicit no-store. Protected responses and shared mapped 400/413 responses use private no-store (deliberate stronger cache restriction than the starter). Unknown failures remain generic private no-store. Summary ownership is `.ai/observability.md`; configuration is `.ai/configuration.md`.
 
 `NOT_APPLICABLE(REQUEST_HANDLER_DECORATOR)`, `NOT_APPLICABLE(WEBSOCKETS)`, `NOT_APPLICABLE(CACHE)`, `NOT_APPLICABLE(JOBS)`, `NOT_APPLICABLE(FILE_TRANSFER)`, `NOT_APPLICABLE(SESSION)`: none adopted. No generic persistence, validators, middleware, framework extensions, or additional runtime dependencies.
+
+Search is omitted for the original unfiltered result. When present it is 1–80 UTF-8 bytes, no ASCII controls/padding, and matches case-sensitive literal substrings in name OR email using SQLite instr. Percent, underscore and SQL-looking text remain data. Null/empty/array/invalid UTF-8/unknown fields fail 400 before SQL. Search is explicitly carried with the same keyset continuation by the caller.
